  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "note",
        "label": {
          "en": "🗺 Cambridge IGCSE 0580 — Syllabus Map",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p style=\"margin:8px 0 4px\"><span class=\"tier-c\">C</span> <strong>Core</strong> topics are examinable on Papers 1 &amp; 3 (Core tier).\n             <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span> <strong>Extended</strong> topics appear on Papers 2 &amp; 4 only.</p><table style=\"font-size:.82rem;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:10px;width:100%\"><tr style=\"background:var(--paper-2)\"><th style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);text-align:left\">ClipSAT Chapter</th><th style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);text-align:left\">0580 Topics covered</th><th style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);text-align:left\">Tier</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">1 Number</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">Types of number, fractions, %, ratio &amp; proportion, standard form, surds, indices, financial maths, limits of accuracy</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\"><span class=\"tier-c\">C</span> <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">2 Algebra &amp; Graphs</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">Expressions, equations, sequences, inequalities, simultaneous equations, graph types</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\"><span class=\"tier-c\">C</span> <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">3 Coordinate Geometry</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">Gradient, midpoint, distance, equation of a line, perpendicular lines</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\"><span class=\"tier-c\">C</span> <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">4 Mensuration</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">Perimeter, area, arc, sector, surface area, volume of 3D shapes</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\"><span class=\"tier-c\">C</span> <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">5 Geometry</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">Angles, polygons, circle theorems, similarity &amp; congruence, construction &amp; loci</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\"><span class=\"tier-c\">C</span> <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">6 Trigonometry</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">SOH-CAH-TOA, sine/cosine rules, area of triangle, bearings, 3D trig</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\"><span class=\"tier-c\">C</span> <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">7 Transformations &amp; Vectors</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">Translation, reflection, rotation, enlargement, column vectors, vector paths, magnitude</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\"><span class=\"tier-c\">C</span> <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">8 Probability &amp; Statistics</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">Probability, tree diagrams, conditional probability, averages, spread, frequency tables, histograms, cumulative frequency, box plots</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\"><span class=\"tier-c\">C</span> <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">9 Functions</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">Function notation, domain, composite, inverse</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\"><span class=\"tier-e\">E</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">10 Sets &amp; Venn Diagrams</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">Set notation, union, intersection, complement, two- and three-set Venn diagrams</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\"><span class=\"tier-c\">C</span> <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">11 Matrices <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span></td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\">Matrix operations, determinant, inverse, solving simultaneous equations</td><td style=\"padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line)\"><span class=\"tier-e\">E</span></td></tr></table>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The numerical backbone of the whole syllabus: working confidently with fractions, percentages, ratio, standard form, indices and rounding. Most marks here are earned by careful, methodical arithmetic rather than clever tricks.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 1.1 — Standard form",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A number is in <strong>standard form</strong> when written as \\( a\\times 10^{n} \\) with \\( 1\\le a&lt;10 \\) and \\( n \\) an integer. Large numbers take a positive \\( n \\); small numbers (less than 1) take a negative \\( n \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Percentage change",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{\\text{change}}{\\text{original}}\\times 100\\% \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Index law 1 — Product",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( a^{m}\\,a^{n}=a^{m+n} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Index law 2 — Quotient",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{a^{m}}{a^{n}}=a^{m-n} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Index law 3 — Power",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (a^{m})^{n}=a^{mn} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Reverse %",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\text{original}=\\dfrac{\\text{new value}}{1\\pm r} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Bounds",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "value rounded to a unit lies within \\( \\pm\\tfrac12 \\) unit",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Write \\( 0.000452 \\) in standard form.</p><p>Move the decimal point four places right to land between 4 and 5, so the exponent is \\( -4 \\):</p>\\[ 0.000452 = 4.52\\times 10^{-4}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A coat costs $60 after a 20% discount. Find its original price.</p><p>The sale price is 80% of the original, so divide rather than add back 20%:</p>\\[ \\text{original}=\\frac{60}{0.8}=\\$75. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Surds <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span>",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A <strong>surd</strong> is an irrational root left in exact form (e.g. \\(\\sqrt{3}\\)). Key rules: \\(\\sqrt{ab}=\\sqrt{a}\\cdot\\sqrt{b}\\); \\(\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{a}}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{a}}{a}\\) (rationalising a denominator). To rationalise \\(\\dfrac{p}{a+\\sqrt{b}}\\), multiply numerator and denominator by the conjugate \\(a-\\sqrt{b}\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Surd product",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(\\sqrt{a}\\cdot\\sqrt{b}=\\sqrt{ab}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Rationalise",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{a}}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{a}}{a}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Compound interest",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(A=P\\!\\left(1+\\dfrac{r}{100}\\right)^{\\!n}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Limits of accuracy",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "lower = \\(x-\\tfrac{1}{2}\\delta\\), upper = \\(x+\\tfrac{1}{2}\\delta\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.C — Surds",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Simplify \\(\\sqrt{48}-\\sqrt{27}\\).</p>\\[\\sqrt{48}=4\\sqrt{3},\\quad\\sqrt{27}=3\\sqrt{3}.\\]\\[\\sqrt{48}-\\sqrt{27}=4\\sqrt{3}-3\\sqrt{3}=\\sqrt{3}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.D — Limits of accuracy",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A length is measured as \\(12.4\\) cm, rounded to 1 d.p. State the upper and lower bounds.</p><p>Half the smallest unit = 0.05. <br>Lower bound: \\(12.35\\) cm. &nbsp; Upper bound: \\(12.45\\) cm.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "£800 is invested at 3.5% compound interest per year. Find the amount after 4 years, to the nearest penny.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(A=800\\left(1+\\frac{3.5}{100}\\right)^4=800\\times1.035^4\\approx800\\times1.1475=£918.00\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
